WEBVTT

﻿1

00:01:04.231 --> 00:01:07.901
"Young Percival, no more than 15,


00:01:07.902 --> 00:01:10.236
from the safety of the thicket,


00:01:10.237 --> 00:01:13.247
watched the knights pass by.


00:01:13.741 --> 00:01:17.980
He perceived they served
a higher calling,


00:01:18.179 --> 00:01:22.015
<i>a calling he felt
stirring within him.</i>


00:01:22.016 --> 00:01:26.219
<i>Percival asked his mother permission
to journey to King Arthur's court</i>


00:01:26.220 --> 00:01:28.491
<i>and seek knighthood.</i>


00:01:29.156 --> 00:01:33.293
<i>His mother had long-feared
this moment would come," Sailor.</i>


00:01:33.294 --> 00:01:38.409
"Nonetheless, she gave her son
blessing to pursue his quest.


00:01:38.732 --> 00:01:44.737
But she warned him, he would
be tested beyond imagination.


00:01:44.738 --> 00:01:49.109
Be deprived, know pain and sadness.


00:01:49.110 --> 00:01:52.587
<i>Perhaps, never become a knight.</i>


00:01:53.147 --> 00:01:56.954
<i>Percival traveled to
King Arthur's court.</i>


00:01:57.118 --> 00:02:00.320
<i>There, he met rebuke and ridicule.</i>


00:02:00.321 --> 00:02:05.903
For he was not of noble birth,
nor did he possess skill of arms.


00:02:06.627 --> 00:02:10.897
<i>In secret, he studied the
ways of the knights.</i>


00:02:10.898 --> 00:02:14.033
<i>His plight caught the
eye of Sir Lancelot</i>


00:02:14.034 --> 00:02:16.475
who began to mentor him.


00:02:19.240 --> 00:02:23.276
<i>During Percival's
ordeal, the Red Knight</i>


00:02:23.277 --> 00:02:29.428
an incarnate of darkness,
sought to destroy the Grail.


00:02:30.484 --> 00:02:35.929
He lay waste to King Arthur's
knights, one by one.


00:02:39.193 --> 00:02:42.962
<i>Finally, it fell upon
slender Percival</i>


00:02:42.963 --> 00:02:46.201
<i>to face the Red Knight."</i>


00:02:47.001 --> 00:02:51.115
<i>And Sailor, "Percival had no fear."</i>


00:02:51.906 --> 00:02:53.106
Get up, Sailor!


00:02:53.107 --> 00:02:55.742
<i>"His years of hardship had
taught him how to suffer.</i>


00:02:55.743 --> 00:02:59.720
<i>He was ready in body,
mind and spirit.</i>


00:03:01.148 --> 00:03:06.821
<i>He would prove in life or death,
his worthiness in battle.</i>


00:03:08.389 --> 00:03:12.859
<i>Percival went forth
with joy in his heart.</i>


00:03:12.860 --> 00:03:17.864
<i>For this was what he wanted:
to be an instrument of peace.</i>


00:03:17.865 --> 00:03:24.641
<i>To be able to sacrifice all
in service of God and man."</i>


00:03:54.134 --> 00:03:56.837
Lead with your right, kid!


00:04:10.050 --> 00:04:11.991
Lay on him. Lay on him!


00:04:18.125 --> 00:04:21.272
- Get away from him.
- Let him go, let him go.


00:04:21.629 --> 00:04:23.831
Let's see some blood!


00:04:28.435 --> 00:04:30.410
Work the body!


00:04:33.907 --> 00:04:36.018
Kill him, Sailor!


00:04:37.344 --> 00:04:40.491
- Come on, let him go.
- Let's see some blood!


00:04:43.417 --> 00:04:46.154
You got him, kid! Take him down!


00:04:51.892 --> 00:04:53.726
You gotta throw back
here, let's go.


00:04:53.727 --> 00:04:55.497
Break it up, boy. Break it up!


00:05:02.569 --> 00:05:05.340
Stop the haymakers. Stop
the haymakers! Double up.


00:05:06.540 --> 00:05:09.108
Another fight, then, is it?


00:05:09.109 --> 00:05:11.789
Once more into the fray.


00:05:12.780 --> 00:05:14.425
Once more into the fray.


00:05:15.716 --> 00:05:18.157
You're a silly man.


00:05:18.385 --> 00:05:21.220
- It's okay, Mom.
- No, it's not okay.


00:05:21.221 --> 00:05:25.391
- I'm not gonna get hurt.
- Yes, you will. You're too old.


00:05:25.392 --> 00:05:28.300
- I'm in good shape.
- No, you're still old.


00:05:28.729 --> 00:05:30.997
I got one or two fights
left in me, right, Ma?


00:05:30.998 --> 00:05:34.236
No, you are used up and broken.


00:05:36.670 --> 00:05:38.271
I've never been knocked down.


00:05:38.272 --> 00:05:41.341
Heh. See, that's why you're broken.


00:05:41.342 --> 00:05:44.455
A man should know when
to go down. You don't.


00:05:46.213 --> 00:05:47.949
You never did.


00:05:50.451 --> 00:05:52.952
I never should have said it to you.


00:05:52.953 --> 00:05:54.153
Said what?


00:05:54.154 --> 00:05:57.223
That I want to go to
Ireland before it comes.


00:05:57.224 --> 00:05:58.732
You didn't, I did.


00:05:59.059 --> 00:06:01.000
You are such a liar.


00:06:03.030 --> 00:06:06.006
Anyways, loser's
purse will cover it.


00:06:07.167 --> 00:06:09.938
Oh. I see you're aiming high.


00:06:16.510 --> 00:06:18.417
Father Brennan wants
to talk to you.


00:06:18.679 --> 00:06:21.257
About what? And don't say God.


00:06:22.182 --> 00:06:23.588
About what's coming.


00:06:24.685 --> 00:06:26.023
I'm not afraid.


00:06:27.955 --> 00:06:30.533
You should pass in a
state of grace, Ma.


00:06:31.458 --> 00:06:33.001
You still believe, don't you?


00:06:35.162 --> 00:06:36.432
Yeah, I do.


00:06:37.431 --> 00:06:40.271
How can you after
what he did to you?


00:06:40.701 --> 00:06:43.575
Only a monster takes the innocent.


00:06:44.238 --> 00:06:47.351
If there is a God, it's a monster.


00:06:47.574 --> 00:06:51.277
A doer of evil and wicked things.


00:06:51.278 --> 00:06:54.580
I will not seek grace
from a monster,


00:06:54.581 --> 00:06:57.489
nor will a monster give it.


00:07:02.289 --> 00:07:04.196
Will you talk to Father Brennan?


00:07:04.691 --> 00:07:08.161
Maybe. If he takes off his robes
and shoves a crucifix up his arse.


00:07:08.162 --> 00:07:09.773
Maybe.


00:07:10.431 --> 00:07:11.666
Nice, Ma.


00:07:13.534 --> 00:07:17.045
- I'll ask him, see what he says.
- Good.


00:07:19.706 --> 00:07:22.742
Have you gone to see Albright?
Will he be there with you?


00:07:22.743 --> 00:07:24.710
- He can't be there.
- Why not?


00:07:24.711 --> 00:07:27.280
He's busy at Safe Hope.


00:07:27.281 --> 00:07:29.549
- I see.
- He's a good man.


00:07:29.550 --> 00:07:32.856
If he was a good man, he would
talk you out of this fight.


00:07:33.554 --> 00:07:36.564
No one's gonna talk me
out of the fight, Ma.


00:07:39.526 --> 00:07:42.764
- Lay it on, Sailor!
- You've already got the game!


00:07:45.399 --> 00:07:47.806
It's all you, Sailor. Come on!


00:07:48.335 --> 00:07:50.811
Use your jab, man. Use your jab.


00:07:51.171 --> 00:07:54.511
Come on, man. Come on! Come on.


00:08:09.590 --> 00:08:11.792
Back to your corners,
guys, let's go.


00:08:11.825 --> 00:08:14.293
- You're done.
- Yeah.


00:08:14.294 --> 00:08:17.763
Hey, kid. Get over here.
Come on, sit down.


00:08:17.764 --> 00:08:19.699
<i>Sailor! Sailor!</i>


00:08:19.700 --> 00:08:23.035
All right, come on, sit down.
You ain't got all day. Come on.


00:08:23.036 --> 00:08:26.172
<i>Sailor! Sailor! Sailor!</i>


00:08:26.173 --> 00:08:28.741
You wanna make it 10 rounds,
you gotta listen to me.


00:08:28.742 --> 00:08:31.310
You're dropping your
right hand, like that.


00:08:31.311 --> 00:08:32.945
Keep your head on his shoulder.


00:08:32.946 --> 00:08:34.280
- Can't you do that?
- Yeah.


00:08:34.281 --> 00:08:38.451
It's time for you to put this old man
down now. You do it now, hear?


00:08:38.452 --> 00:08:40.219
- Yes, sir.
- No more fooling around.


00:08:40.220 --> 00:08:43.155
That's enough of this nonsense.
You're young, man, and fast.


00:08:43.156 --> 00:08:45.859
Put him down so we can
go home, all right?


00:08:50.397 --> 00:08:53.266
Let's take a look,
Sailor. How's that eye?


00:08:53.267 --> 00:08:55.434
- Good, doc. It's good.
- Are you sure?


00:08:55.435 --> 00:08:56.669
- Yeah.
- All right.


00:08:56.670 --> 00:08:59.272
That opens up anymore,
I'm gonna stop the fight.


00:08:59.273 --> 00:09:02.545
- I'll do my best, doc.
- Do the best you can.


00:09:03.810 --> 00:09:05.411
Oh, great.


00:09:05.412 --> 00:09:07.980
Hey, King's fine. You check
that old man over there.


00:09:07.981 --> 00:09:10.957
- He ain't so fine.
- Back off, Cubby.


00:09:11.618 --> 00:09:14.687
- Looking better than Sailor.
- I'm fine.


00:09:14.688 --> 00:09:17.266
Didn't think you
could take a punch.


00:09:17.524 --> 00:09:20.295
- I can take a punch.
- You're proving it, kid.


00:09:21.862 --> 00:09:24.975
You're gonna get up close so
you can do some damage, okay?


00:09:27.634 --> 00:09:29.438
Concentrate.


00:09:34.875 --> 00:09:36.520
I wanna have it.


00:09:37.444 --> 00:09:40.022
You don't know what that means.


00:09:40.514 --> 00:09:42.489
Yes, I do.


00:09:42.649 --> 00:09:45.418
- No, you don't.
- It means work.


00:09:45.419 --> 00:09:47.687
It means money.


00:09:47.688 --> 00:09:51.131
- I can make money.
- How?


00:09:52.893 --> 00:09:55.266
Well, I can box.


00:09:56.663 --> 00:09:59.139
And I have some modeling jobs too.


00:09:59.633 --> 00:10:01.244
We're too young.


00:10:02.769 --> 00:10:06.678
- Too young for what?
- To have a baby.


00:10:08.408 --> 00:10:10.776
I wanna spend the rest
of my life with you.


00:10:10.777 --> 00:10:12.945
- No, you don't.
- Yes, I do.


00:10:12.946 --> 00:10:15.314
- No, you don't.
- I wanna marry you.


00:10:15.315 --> 00:10:19.725
I wanna marry you right
now. This morning.


00:10:20.821 --> 00:10:23.558
And I'll take care
of you and our baby.


00:10:24.891 --> 00:10:27.537
I promise you that.


00:10:30.330 --> 00:10:32.601
We have a family.


00:10:33.767 --> 00:10:36.948
I've never had that before.


00:10:39.573 --> 00:10:41.548
Me neither.


00:10:43.343 --> 00:10:45.682
Let's have our baby.


00:10:52.152 --> 00:10:53.797
Okay.


00:10:55.622 --> 00:10:56.960
Okay.


00:10:57.357 --> 00:10:59.230
Okay.


00:11:01.561 --> 00:11:03.263
But, King...


00:11:06.299 --> 00:11:09.412
I wanna give this baby
something besides life.


00:11:09.803 --> 00:11:11.277
What?


00:11:13.173 --> 00:11:16.479
I wanna give it something
it can be proud of.


00:11:18.612 --> 00:11:22.615
You keep him at a distance with
that jab. You dance around, huh?


00:11:22.616 --> 00:11:26.052
That man throws some wild
hooks, you know? Duck.


00:11:26.053 --> 00:11:29.021
Stop. You cannot win a fight
laying on a guy, okay?


00:11:29.022 --> 00:11:31.323
So let's win it. You
cannot outmuscle this kid.


00:11:31.324 --> 00:11:33.826
You cannot outfight him
and you can't outrun him.


00:11:33.827 --> 00:11:37.129
But you outweigh him and you can
outthink him. You wanna win it?


00:11:37.130 --> 00:11:39.398
- Yeah.
- You're the heavier one, lay on him.


00:11:39.399 --> 00:11:43.803
Keep your head on the right side of him.
Let the kid get cocky. Listen to me.


00:11:43.804 --> 00:11:46.572
Hey. Hey. What are you doing?


00:11:46.573 --> 00:11:49.208
What the hell's the matter?
You wanna win the fight?


00:11:49.209 --> 00:11:52.244
Keep your head on that right
shoulder. Once you get that rhythm,


00:11:52.245 --> 00:11:55.289
setup, he drops down,
you cross him, okay?


00:12:10.097 --> 00:12:14.166
Cubby. And what's this
I hear about King?


00:12:14.167 --> 00:12:16.635
I'm gonna give the
kid another chance.


00:12:16.636 --> 00:12:19.872
- King is a screwup.
- No, no, he's all cleaned up now.


00:12:19.873 --> 00:12:23.709
- The kid does have talent. Real talent.
- Yeah, he's always had talent.


00:12:23.710 --> 00:12:25.544
I poured a lot of money into him,


00:12:25.545 --> 00:12:27.980
and you gotta have it
to go with that talent.


00:12:27.981 --> 00:12:31.751
- Yeah, well, he's going to have a baby.
- There's a disaster waiting to happen.


00:12:31.752 --> 00:12:34.353
He got married to a
nice, young girl.


00:12:34.354 --> 00:12:36.789
He was my fighter before
you stole him from me.


00:12:36.790 --> 00:12:38.791
I did not steal him. Hey, look.


00:12:38.792 --> 00:12:41.293
You've got that night
coming up at the Lion Head?


00:12:41.294 --> 00:12:44.304
- Yeah.
- I want you to get King a fight there.


00:12:44.531 --> 00:12:47.466
- Maybe as an undercard.
- No, no, no, main event.


00:12:47.467 --> 00:12:52.071
- What? Look, King is no main event.
- Yes, he is.


00:12:52.072 --> 00:12:55.481
I'll put up the purse, man.
Ten-thousand dollars.


00:12:55.542 --> 00:12:56.742
Ten rounds.


00:12:56.743 --> 00:12:58.978
You really think he has
his head on straight?


00:12:58.979 --> 00:13:00.980
Yes. Yes, yes, yes.


00:13:00.981 --> 00:13:02.848
All right, I'll take
a piece of him.


00:13:02.849 --> 00:13:05.785
No, no, no. Ha, ha.
He doesn't like you.


00:13:05.786 --> 00:13:08.420
- I'll take 50 percent of him.
- He's not for sale.


00:13:08.421 --> 00:13:11.524
Hey, look, you know he was
my fighter before you took him.


00:13:11.525 --> 00:13:18.030
I didn't steal him. Hey, you know why
all your fighters leave you, man? Huh?


00:13:18.031 --> 00:13:20.432
- Because you steal them from me.
- Yeah.


00:13:20.433 --> 00:13:25.404
Same reason why your wife left you.
The same reason why I left you.


00:13:25.405 --> 00:13:27.640
Just give me a piece of the kid.


00:13:27.641 --> 00:13:29.377
Hey, look.


00:13:32.946 --> 00:13:35.514
You line up something for King, hm?


00:13:35.515 --> 00:13:38.184
Someone the kid could handle, huh?


00:13:38.185 --> 00:13:43.189
More than just a warm body,
but somebody he could beat, huh?


00:13:43.190 --> 00:13:45.057
I want it kept local.


00:13:45.058 --> 00:13:48.467
I don't wanna bear the expense
of bringing somebody in here.


00:13:49.329 --> 00:13:51.063
What about Charlie Simms?


00:13:51.064 --> 00:13:54.438
No, he's in prison. Armed robbery.


00:13:54.768 --> 00:13:56.368
Teddy Bigfoot?


00:13:56.369 --> 00:13:59.205
Teddy Bigfoot? Teddy Bigfoot,
man, he's a lot of Bigfoot.


00:13:59.206 --> 00:14:01.010
Man, he's 350 pounds now.


00:14:03.076 --> 00:14:05.177
- Bigfoot, yeah.
- Yeah.


00:14:05.178 --> 00:14:06.880
Hey.


00:14:07.514 --> 00:14:09.318
How about Sailor O'Connor?


00:14:09.382 --> 00:14:10.890
- Sailor?
- Yeah.


00:14:11.484 --> 00:14:13.129
Is he still fighting?


00:14:14.154 --> 00:14:16.188
No, but it might not really matter.


00:14:16.189 --> 00:14:19.191
I mean, if I could get him
to take one more fight.


00:14:19.192 --> 00:14:21.760
- People loved him.
- Yeah, yeah, he was very popular.


00:14:21.761 --> 00:14:24.630
Everybody wanted to see if he
was gonna get knocked down.


00:14:24.631 --> 00:14:27.132
- Yeah.
- And every fighter wanted to be the first.


00:14:27.133 --> 00:14:28.868
That's a good hook, man.


00:14:28.869 --> 00:14:30.769
Yeah, that'd be big if King


00:14:30.770 --> 00:14:34.039
could knock Sailor down. Heh.


00:14:34.040 --> 00:14:36.508
- That's good.
- Yeah. I'm gonna run it by King.


00:14:36.509 --> 00:14:38.110
- I'll talk to Sailor.
- Yup.


00:14:38.111 --> 00:14:41.547
- Hey, I want a piece of the kid.
- Not going to happen, man.


00:14:41.548 --> 00:14:44.483
- Well, we'll see.
- Yeah, yeah.


00:15:04.604 --> 00:15:06.784
<i>Why should we bother
to go see the doctor?</i>


00:15:07.040 --> 00:15:08.741
What's there to talk about?


00:15:08.742 --> 00:15:11.855
If you're dying, you're dying.
I know I'm dying.


00:15:14.014 --> 00:15:15.887
How do you know?


00:15:17.250 --> 00:15:21.557
Tell me you wouldn't know if you
were rotting from the inside out.


00:15:26.593 --> 00:15:27.793
It's cancer.


00:15:27.794 --> 00:15:31.339
Cancer, rot, no difference.


00:15:31.431 --> 00:15:32.666
Ma...


00:15:32.666 --> 00:15:37.136
Aw. Don't get all melancholy on me.


00:15:37.137 --> 00:15:40.306
I think it'd be good if you and I
went and saw a doctor together.


00:15:40.307 --> 00:15:44.512
- Yeah, well, you go see him if you want.
- Ma, there may be some pain.


00:15:46.813 --> 00:15:48.822
How long did he say I have?


00:15:49.749 --> 00:15:51.784
- Ma.
- Oh, don't be such a baby.


00:15:51.785 --> 00:15:53.726
How long did he say I have?


00:15:56.690 --> 00:15:58.164
Six months.


00:16:01.561 --> 00:16:03.104
I'm sorry.


00:16:04.264 --> 00:16:05.602
Sorry for what?


00:16:08.134 --> 00:16:10.814
No one's getting out alive.


00:16:15.475 --> 00:16:17.712
Is there anything I can do for you?


00:16:21.081 --> 00:16:26.697
Well, it might be nice to take one
last trip to Ireland before it comes.


00:16:27.420 --> 00:16:30.965
That'd be nice. Maybe you and me.


00:16:33.493 --> 00:16:35.195
Yeah.


00:16:43.503 --> 00:16:45.170
King, come on.


00:16:45.171 --> 00:16:47.351
Go box. Go box!


00:16:48.008 --> 00:16:49.448
Let's go home.


00:17:27.080 --> 00:17:30.549
<i>She's been in for five years.
She's asked me to be there</i>


00:17:30.550 --> 00:17:33.697
- for her parole hearing.
- You gonna go?


00:17:33.853 --> 00:17:35.589
I don't know.


00:17:36.890 --> 00:17:41.561
I've gotten to know her a lot better
through the letters that she sent me.


00:17:42.062 --> 00:17:45.402
She wants to speak with
you if she gets out.


00:17:46.032 --> 00:17:47.836
I can't do that.


00:17:50.136 --> 00:17:51.781
You can try.


00:17:53.173 --> 00:17:56.183
Sean, I don't have it in me.


00:17:58.812 --> 00:18:02.255
Sailor, her loss is
as great as yours.


00:18:04.184 --> 00:18:05.829
Is it?


00:18:06.853 --> 00:18:11.900
I'm sorry. Loss can't be measured.


00:18:12.859 --> 00:18:15.505
No. No, it can't.


00:18:17.931 --> 00:18:20.771
Do you want her to
continue to suffer?


00:18:28.074 --> 00:18:29.808
Do you


00:18:29.809 --> 00:18:33.047
want her to continue to suffer?


00:18:35.048 --> 00:18:37.922
Yeah. I think I do.


00:18:38.518 --> 00:18:40.595
Don't you think she's
suffered enough?


00:18:40.887 --> 00:18:45.661
Sean, I thought we agreed,
you can't measure suffering.


00:18:48.895 --> 00:18:52.076
Do you have no pity for her?


00:18:52.765 --> 00:18:56.503
You know, my ma has a
saying about pity:


00:18:57.403 --> 00:19:00.606
Pity arrests the heart


00:19:00.607 --> 00:19:03.344
and unites it with those
who have wronged us.


00:19:04.110 --> 00:19:06.415
I need to go see Rose.


00:19:07.480 --> 00:19:09.648
Won't do any good,
she's at war with God.


00:19:09.649 --> 00:19:11.294
Yeah.


00:19:13.486 --> 00:19:16.121
You taking confessions
today, Father?


00:19:16.122 --> 00:19:18.632
You have nothing to confess,


00:19:18.725 --> 00:19:22.027
other than what we
just talked about.


00:19:28.301 --> 00:19:29.946
Yes.


